ing our queen into  the mix and after he moves his knight  for safety we can go ahead and capture  with our knight here and if he then  recaptures with his knight we can then  take with either our queen or rook and  the King will be in check so very good  situation for us and this right here is  one of the most common opening looks  that you'll see from the roy lopez if  you're playing the non exchange  variation if you're playing the exchange  variation obviously the knight and the  bishop will not be here and you'll have  double pawns on the c file but from this  variation it's very straightforward  black's going to continue with eise evan  he's going to castle white is going to  develop eventually there's going to be  an attack on the  black kingside depending on where black  moves white can develop and there's not  again I'll said there's not a lot of  trickeration in this it's pretty  straightforward it's fine  tactics are gonna win this game  sometimes it can be somewhat boring as  you can see there hasn't been one piece  that's been captured so far but if you  rule enjoy chess and really enjoy out  thinking your opponent on every move  this is a very good opening so hope this  was helpful hope you learned a lot from  the roy lopez there's many variations  that we're actually going to get into in  some of the later videos but please  subscribe you can find out when the new  videos come out I have quite a few  videos coming out in the near future so  check out the website it's going to be  actually launching at the end of this  week March 20th so hope you all enjoyed  and see you next video

